# Line endings and binary files (issue #11, repository hygiene).
#
# The repository stores text normalized (LF); every checkout gets CRLF for
# the Delphi and Windows files below - independent of the committer's
# core.autocrlf. LF-only sources are not cosmetic: the debugger can put
# breakpoints on the wrong lines (the plugin's own "Debug consistency" check
# reports them for exactly that reason).
#
# Encoding: the sources are UTF-8 WITH BOM. There is deliberately no
# working-tree-encoding here - UTF-8 to UTF-8 would convert nothing; the BOM
# and the CRLF state are guarded by the DUnitX test TRepoHygieneTests
# (Tests\Test.RepoHygiene.pas).

# anything not listed: Git decides text/binary, line endings follow autocrlf
*            text=auto

# Delphi sources and projects
*.pas        text eol=crlf
*.inc        text eol=crlf
*.dpr        text eol=crlf
*.dpk        text eol=crlf
*.dproj      text eol=crlf
*.groupproj  text eol=crlf
*.dof        text eol=crlf
*.cfg        text eol=crlf

# form files: TEXT forms get CRLF, a BINARY form (NUL bytes) must never be
# converted - text=auto lets Git look at the content first
*.dfm        text=auto eol=crlf
*.fmx        text=auto eol=crlf

# scripts and documents
*.cmd        text eol=crlf
*.bat        text eol=crlf
*.ps1        text eol=crlf
*.xml        text eol=crlf
*.md         text eol=crlf
*.txt        text eol=crlf
*.json       text eol=crlf

# binaries
*.res        binary
*.dcu        binary
*.dcp        binary
*.bpl        binary
*.exe        binary
*.dll        binary
*.ico        binary
*.png        binary
*.bmp        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.zip        binary
